## Destroy Behavior

{{- if .Resource.DestroyDisables}}
Destroy performs a fresh GET, preserves the complete response, sets `template=false` and `configs.status=false`, sends the complete PUT, and verifies the normalized GET response before Terraform removes the resource from state.
{{- else if .Resource.TemplateDestroyCoupledFields}}
Destroy forgets this app-scoped resource without sending a disabling PUT. The remote application {{.Resource.OperationName}} configuration remains unchanged and Terraform emits a warning. This behavior does not apply to `fortiappseccloud_waf_template_{{.Resource.TypeNameSuffix | trimWAFPrefix}}`, which disables the template module by setting its reviewed top-level, cache, and compression statuses false together.
{{- else if .Resource.TemplateDestroyDisables}}
Destroy forgets this app-scoped resource without sending a disabling PUT. The remote application {{.Resource.OperationName}} configuration remains unchanged and Terraform emits a warning. This behavior does not apply to `fortiappseccloud_waf_template_{{.Resource.TypeNameSuffix | trimWAFPrefix}}`, which disables the template module before Terraform removes it from state.
{{- else}}
Destroy forgets this resource without sending a disabling PUT. The remote {{.Resource.OperationName}} configuration remains unchanged and Terraform emits a warning.
{{- end}}
